{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Adjusted to work with the modified ReaTooled Hover Edit Mode script ("_RS7cb08a92f7a211ce66734644b4fbe99a91bd42f5")\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 TJF Add Strech Marker (Hover Mode Dependant)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Will add Stretch Markers at Mouse Cursor or Edit Curser depending on Hover Mode Status Recommend Assign to "W" key\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Adjusted to work with the modified ReaTooled Hover Edit Mode script ("_RS7cb08a92f7a211ce66734644b4fbe99a91bd42f5")\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 TJF TJF Add Sync Point (Hover Mode Dependent)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Will also not split if no item is selected. Mimics "CMD + ," in protools Adds Hover Mode Support\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Converts an existing butt joint at the edit cursor into a centered crossfade using REAPER's default crossfade length. WARNING: This necessarily modifies item boundaries (by design).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Clears all take envelopes and resets item and take volume to 0.0dB for all selected items / takes.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Like Pro Tools' "Coalesce Clip Gain to Volume Automation"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 For each selected item, moves its clip gain into the track's volume automation and resets the clip gain to 0 dB. Clip gain here means the take volume envelope, plus (see SETTINGS) the take volume and item volume. Writes to the Pre-FX volume envelope by default, and creates it if needed. Short glides at the item edges keep the automation outside the item as it was. Known limit: two selected items overlapping on the same track can give unexpected results. Envelopes with automation items are skipped.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Like Pro Tools' "Coalesce Volume Automation to Clip Gain"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 For each selected item, moves the track's volume automation under the item into the item's take volume envelope (combined with any clip gain already there), and sets the track automation to 0 dB across the item. Uses the Pre-FX volume envelope by default. Creates the take volume envelope if needed. Short glides at the item edges keep the automation outside the item as it was. Known limit: two selected items overlapping on the same track can give unexpected results. Envelopes with automation items are skipped.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Creates a unified razor area from all razor edits (min start to max end), applies it to all tracks, and sets matching time selection. If no razor exists, falls back to time selection. Exits silently if neither is set.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Creates a track-area Razor Edit that exactly spans the empty space (gap) surrounding the edit cursor on a target track. Target track resolution (in order of preference): 1) Track under mouse (native hit-test; pinned-track safe), else 2) Track under mouse via SWS (fallback), else 3) Single selected track, else 4) Last touched track. Handles edge cases:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Gap from project start (0) to the first item\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Gap from the last item to project end\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Tracks with no items (entire project length) Project end is resolved in order of priority: 1) Marker named "=END" 2) Explicit Project Settings end time ("PROJECT_LENGTH") 3) Automatic length (GetProjectLength) If no gap encompasses the edit cursor (e.g., cursor is inside an item), no changes are made.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Waits for REAPER to apply a time or loop selection (useful when triggered by mouse modifiers), then creates razor edit areas across all tracks and matches time selection.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Creates a track-area Razor Edit from the edit cursor to the end of the project. If no tracks are selected, applies to ALL tracks. Replaces existing Razor on those tracks. If \u8805?1 track is selected AND helper (_RSf28451a9bd28e7b3d270c4e5ce58052377a5e3df) is NOT running, ignore the selected tracks and apply ONLY to the focused (last-touched) track.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Creates a track-area Razor Edit from project start (0.0) to the edit cursor. If no tracks are selected, applies to ALL tracks. If at least one track is selected AND the helper script (_RSf28451a9bd28e7b3d270c4e5ce58052377a5e3df) is NOT running, ignore selected tracks and apply ONLY to the focused (last touched) track.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 This script creates an empty MIDI item from the time selection and ads a tone generator JS effect to the item -- good for "beeping out" sections of audio.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Creates or extends a razor edit area across multiple tracks.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Behavior:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 - No razor exists anywhere: creates razor from pre-click cursor to mouse on selected tracks.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 - Razor exists, mouse is on a track with a razor, mouse is outside union bounds:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 extends union bounds toward mouse, writes to all tracks with a razor.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 - Razor exists, mouse is on a track with a razor, mouse is inside union bounds:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 trims nearest edge of union bounds to mouse position, writes to all tracks with a razor.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 - Razor exists, mouse is on a track without a razor:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 adds that track to the razor group using existing union bounds unchanged.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Requires ReaTooled - Link Razor Area to Item Selection (Context-Aware) v4.6+ to be running.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Assign to a left-click mouse modifier in Arrange view.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Behavior priority: 1) If any Razor Edit(s) exist on any track:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Extend those exact track-area Razor segments (guid == "") to the track(s) directly above the tracks that have them. (Optionally propagate env/item GUID segments if enabled.) 2) Else, if items are selected:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Create Razor segments that match each selected item (per-item, per-track), and also apply those segments to the track(s) directly above. 3) Else, if a time selection exists and it intersects selected items:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab For each selected item, create a Razor segment from the intersection of the item bounds and the time selection, then mirror to the track(s) above. Finish rules (family-consistent):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Always clear the Time Selection at the end.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab If LINK is OFF, restore Loop Points to their original position (Razor edits remain).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab If LINK is ON, clearing TS will also clear LP (we do not toggle LINK).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Behavior priority: 1) If any Razor Edit(s) exist on any track:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Extend those exact track-area Razor segments (guid == "") to the track(s) directly below the tracks that have them. (Optionally propagate env/item GUID segments if enabled.) 2) Else, if items are selected:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Create Razor segments that match each selected item (per-item, per-track), and also apply those segments to the track(s) directly below. 3) Else, if a time selection exists and it intersects selected items:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab For each selected item, create a Razor segment from the intersection of the item bounds and the time selection, then mirror to the track(s) below. Finish rules (family-consistent):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Always clear the Time Selection at the end.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab If LINK is OFF, restore Loop Points to their original position (Razor edits remain).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab If LINK is ON, clearing TS will also clear LP (we do not toggle LINK).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Depending on the state of the ReaTooled Toggle Tab to Transient button,\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 this script creates or extends a time selection + razor area to the next (right) transient or item edge.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 It replicates SHIFT+TAB / SHIFT+' behavior from Pro Tools, with gap-aware stepping.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Depending on the state of the ReaTooled Toggle Tab to Transient button,\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 this script creates or extends a time selection + razor area to the previous (left) transient or item edge.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Mirrors the rightward version, including fade/crossfade-aware stepping and robust viewport follow of the left edge.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Adjusted to work with the modified ReaTooled Hover Edit Mode script ("_RS7cb08a92f7a211ce66734644b4fbe99a91bd42f5")\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 TJF Fade In to Edit Cursor or Mouse (Hover Mode Dependant)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Depending on Status of Hover mode will either fade in to edit cursor or mouse cursor Recommend Assigning to "D" key\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Adjusted to work with the modified ReaTooled Hover Edit Mode script ("_RS7cb08a92f7a211ce66734644b4fbe99a91bd42f5")\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 TJF Fade Out from Edit Cursor or Mouse (Hover Mode Dependant)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Depending on Status of Hover mode will either fade out from edit cursor or mouse cursor Recommend Assigning to "G" key\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Reatooled version that preserves the original behavior (Time Selection, Razor Edit, Item Selection, Take/Track envelopes, Automation Items, optional Edit Cursor pickup), with safer logic and performance improvements:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab No mutation of shared state across loops (per-AI/local clamping)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Optional filters for envelope visibility and arming\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Fewer redundant Envelope_Evaluate calls (re-evaluate only when needed)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Sort once per AI batch, not per-point\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Safer clamping for item-relative cursor\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Cleaner structure and locals NOTE: This script uses only native ReaScript API (no SWS BR_ calls).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Glue items and keep handles, like Pro Tools AudioSuite rendering\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Opens a small window (it remembers your last choices):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab File mode: "Create continuous file" glues the selected items on each track into one item; "Create individual files" glues each item on its own\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Handle length in seconds (default 2), or press "Whole File" to keep all the source audio Render (or Enter) glues, Cancel (or Esc) closes. The window can stay open while you change the selection. The glued item stays exactly where and as long as the original selection, but its new file has extra audio beyond its edges, so you can still trim it out afterwards. Like REAPER's own glue, take FX and take envelopes are printed. Handles only reach as far as the source audio exists (and not before the project start). Fades at the outer edges are kept; crossfades inside a continuous glue are printed as they are. Works with fixed item lanes (one item per lane). Needs ReaImGui (installed with ReaTooled).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Grid and nudge settings, like Pro Tools' Edit window\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Turn the grid on and off, choose its division, and set the nudge amount and unit, in a dockable window or right inside REAPER's Transport bar.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Grid: click to toggle the grid; the division menu has frame rate, 1 measure and musical divisions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Nudge: click the value to type one; the unit menu has milliseconds, seconds, measures and beats (with dotted and triplet), samples, frames and more.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab In the Transport (right-click the window > Put in the Transport): Grid above Nudge (or one row), sharp on Retina/HiDPI screens and drawn in your theme's colors. Drag the grip to move it along the Transport and its right edge to resize it; the grip's menu attaches it to an edge of the Transport, either side of the time display or left of the selection display, locks it, or puts it back in a window.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab It moves and resizes with the Transport, never covers the transport buttons or time display, moves to free space when it runs out of room, and hides when there is none. Mapped to M. Starts with REAPER, in the window or the Transport, whichever you used last.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Turns a razor edit (or time selection) into a looping, click-free\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 section and copies it, ready to paste as room tone. 1. Sets the time selection to the razor edit areas (if there are any) 2. Splits the item at the nearest zero crossings to the start and end 3. Turns on "Loop source" for the section and loops that part of the source 4. Smart-copies it Replaces the custom action of the same name, without needing the TJF and Lokasenna scripts it used.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Pro Tools-like TAB using ReaTooled "Toggle Tab to Transient".\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Transient mode (toggle ON):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Uses REAPER\u8217?s native transient navigation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Temporarily saves/restores item selection using Selection Set #01.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Respects user track/item selection context (tracks > all items).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Item-edge mode (toggle OFF):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Moves between fades, crossfades, item edges on relevant tracks.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab No selection changes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab View centers on edit cursor only if it moves off-screen (margin configurable).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab No defer; Undo suppressed (-1).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Pro Tools-like TAB using ReaTooled "Toggle Tab to Transient".\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Transient mode (toggle ON):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Uses REAPER\u8217?s native transient navigation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Temporarily saves/restores item selection using Selection Set #01.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Respects user track/item selection context (tracks > all items).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Item-edge mode (toggle OFF):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Moves between fades, crossfades, item edges on relevant tracks.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab No selection changes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab View centers on edit cursor only if it moves off-screen (margin configurable).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab No defer; Undo suppressed (-1).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Replaces selection with the item under the mouse (no 40529), expands to group via 40034 only if the user's 41156 option is ON, then moves the edit cursor to the earliest start of the current selection. If the link script (_RSed328eb507619b18c1154efa1b048d816cfc2d0c) is ON, also sets loop points to the full span of the selected items. UI stays frozen until the end; view is preserved. Razor mode (set CLICK_MAKES_RAZOR = true below): instead of moving the edit cursor and loop points, the click puts a razor area exactly over the selected item(s), and the Link Timeline and Edit Selection toggle decides whether the loop points follow it. Trade-offs: while the razor area is there, dragging in it does nothing, and with "Razor edits in media item lane affect all track envelopes" on, deleting also deletes the automation under it.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
