{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Renders selected items in place (baking take FX to audio) while preserving the original items with their full FX chain intact on a new hidden archive lane. Archive lanes are timestamped and named with the baked FX chain. Only the main render lane remains visible and plays. Mutes archived items to save CPU.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 IMPORTANT - For rendered files to be named with FX chain info: In REAPER's Render to File dialog, set the filename pattern to use $take as the token. The script names each rendered take after rendering so the output file will automatically be named e.g. "Guitar - EQ2 > Decapitator > H-Reverb.wav"\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
