{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Follows REAPER's "Stop playback at end of loop if repeat is disabled" (stopendofloop): \u8211? ON : REAPER stops at the loop end itself; this script only does the cleanup below, and only when playback really ended at the loop end (not when you press stop). \u8211? OFF: playback carries on past the loop end, and this script does nothing (the cursor and loop points stay where they are).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab \u9654? Play Marker is a singleton and is always forced to {\b ID 0}: \u8211? If ID 0 is occupied (marker or region), it is faithfully recreated at a new auto ID, then removed. \u8211? \u9654? is then created/moved at ID 0 and any other \u9654? by {\b name} are deleted (no color matching).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab LP+EC-aware loop-end cleanup (unchanged semantics, renamed): \u8211? Follow OFF + LP+EC OFF: EDIT := loop start; preserve LP & Razor; \u9654? mirrors LP start (via watcher). \u8211? Follow ON  + LP+EC OFF: \u9654? := loop end; clear LP; keep Razor; EDIT stays. \u8211? Follow ON  + LP+EC ON : EDIT := loop end; clear LP & Razor.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab When LP+EC is OFF and loop points change, \u9654? mirrors Loop Start (queued while playing).\par}
}

