{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Like Pro Tools' Pre/Post-Roll switch (Cmd+K): turns REAPER's pre-roll on playback and pre-roll on recording on or off together. If either is off, both go on; if both are on, both go off. The toolbar button is lit while it's on. While pre-roll is on, a white "Pre-roll" marker shows where playback will really start: the pre-roll length before the play start, moved back to the bar line at or before it when REAPER's "Start pre-roll at start of measure" is checked (a point just before a bar line counts as that bar, within a 16th note, as REAPER does). The play start is worked out like ReaTooled's Play-Stop does it (the loop points if there are any, else the \u9654? play marker when Link Timeline and Edit Selection is off, else the edit cursor). It follows as those move, hides while playing or recording (like \u9654?), and is removed when pre-roll goes off. Drag the marker to change the pre-roll length, like Pro Tools' pre-roll flag: with "Start pre-roll at start of measure" checked it snaps to whole bars (REAPER only starts on a bar line then), unchecked to quarter bars. Needs SWS. Option+click the toolbar button (or Option+run it) to open REAPER's Metronome/pre-roll settings (pre-roll length, etc.) without switching anything. REAPER's own separate toggles still work: turning both off there ends this too.\par}
}

