\widowctrl\hyphauto
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Try and choose scroll and wheel-zoom directions\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Shows REAPER's vertical and horizontal scroll direction (Preferences > Keyboard/Multitouch) and the direction of ReaTooled's wheel scripts (zoom, take volume, pitch, peaks gain), with what each choice does. Every choice takes effect right away, so you can try it in REAPER while the window is open. "Put back how it was" returns all three to what they were when the window opened. Your Mac's own scrolling setting is read, never changed. Opens once after "Set up ReaTooled"; run it any time from the Actions list. Needs ReaImGui and SWS (both installed with ReaTooled).\par}
}

